{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"beryl-orange-oropendola","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Extend the survived-LLM-step-failure tally to review-code and verify-completion\n\n`eclectic-industrial-argali` (61a1-ee49-3c42-4b09) added a run-scoped sink\n(`src/rebar/llm/step_failures.py`) that counts LLM step calls which fail but do not fail the\nrun, and surfaced it on the plan-review verdict as `coverage.llm_step_failures`. That change\nwas deliberately scoped to `review-plan`, the gate where the motivating incident occurred\n(three overlap-judge batches dying, ~15 minutes of wall time, nothing visible in the JSON).\n\nThe same blindness still exists in the other two code-reading gates.\n\n## What is left\n\n- **`review-code`** — already has a `coverage` object\n  (`src/rebar/schemas/code_review_verdict.schema.json`), so this is mostly wiring: activate\n  `collect_step_failures()` in the code-review run scope (the second scope in\n  `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`, alongside `review_kernel.collect_contract_violations()`)\n  and drain into that gate coverage with the same present-only-when-non-empty posture.\n- **`verify-completion`** — has NO `coverage` object at all\n  (`src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json` carries `verdict`, `findings`,\n  `criteria`, `summary`, `remediation`, `target`, `reviewers`, `certifiable`, `runner`,\n  `model`, `trace_id`). It therefore needs a decision about where a tally belongs before any\n  wiring, which is why it was not folded into the parent change.\n\nThe recording site needs no change: every LLM call already funnels through the one seam in\n`PydanticAIRunner.run`, so both gates start counting the moment a scope is active around them.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Observability only, same constraints as the parent: never changes a verdict, an exit code,\n  a signature, or a provenance stamp, and no swallow site changes behaviour.\n- Keep the attestation-safety posture: present ONLY when non-empty, so a clean run stays\n  byte-identical.","id":"fba8-5271-add6-4603","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Tally survived LLM step failures in review-code and verify-completion"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786516301218444001,"uuid":"494cc802-5f54-415d-a3af-2d5e93c32c45"}